claims.claim:
What each mirror contains:
(a) the store window: one map of the WHOLE store object, fb_len = layout.fb_length;
(b) the guest-RAM window: one map of the whole guest-memfd OS-descriptor object;
(c) a ring-region reservation [1 TiB-4 GiB, 1 TiB), where rings are mapped only by a Translated birth;
(d) the mirrored guest rows, FIXED at the guest's own VAs as slices of the store or RAM object;
(e) SKED message-kind placements, which are also guest-leaf driven;
(f) host RM's own GR context buffers, in the host hole [1 TiB-64 GiB, 1 TiB) of any twin with a GR channel.
